From 1b48aa8c181d5d5c01e42b53c7448405505f2ed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <info@fvanmaele.de>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:50:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] [clangd] Index navigation: ignore a shard indexed with
 another command

The shard's positions are checked against the file's content, but not
against the compile command it was indexed with. After a CMake preset
switch or a changed -D the stored shard may record other #ifdef branches
until the file is indexed again, so navigation from the index answered for
the old configuration. A main file's shard stores its command; navigation
from the index now answers only when it equals the current one
(shardCommandMatches).
